# Python Coding Style

- Follow existing project style in `app/` and `main.py` (match neighbors).
- Prefer type annotations on new/changed function signatures.
- Do not introduce black/ruff/isort tooling unless already configured in repo.
- Prefer small, focused diffs; no drive-by refactors.
- See skill `python-patterns` for idioms; prefer existing modules over greenfield layouts.
